{"title":"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Zoran Sunik</i>) A mathematical frog jumps along the number line. The frog starts at 1, and jumps according to the following rule: if the frog is at integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then it can jump either to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/4948eb6c7b0070d6c560380e4b8aa8324dc0932a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2^{m_n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa7675310996f37589003b32e49e94315a7b19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m_n}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the largest power of 2 that is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is a positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is a nonnegative integer, then the minimum number of jumps needed to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b02852649c50d92f54657e47ef1c684ae99b48b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i k$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> is greater than the minimum number of jumps needed to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b92d67419c77c7a9bab9103274256eb1ba428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i$\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7ce4224bc96abb2186db4e92f3e6f35c4e1be23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c779d0ba2c47e7587d30a6d8c860c8d24603fa32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f2990ee6826360c43a2733a21c78b90b8ebcba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i,k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> denote the minimum number of jumps needed to reach the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7009212552fa8ecb383dce7c808ee8900c66e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{i,k} = 2^i k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />. We must prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c3afdd6875bd736bb996d56f7594cf62b27658.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i,k} &gt; x_{i,1}\\qquad\\qquad (1)\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\nfor all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7ce4224bc96abb2186db4e92f3e6f35c4e1be23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a0ef476cf5452cdb5a980c9697dc1068e0731b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. We prove this using the method of descent.\n</p><p>First note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0920fc9da3d00c8ef2bd7b6be6da86400697c822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 0$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a0ef476cf5452cdb5a980c9697dc1068e0731b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, because it takes 0 jumps to reach the starting value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea7fc971bb5d14d4b2ffbd79c0f1bb6ce00bcec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0,1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, and at least one jump to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e4387f000b9db2ab1c2e3e37ddaeadd845d8486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{0,k} = k\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Now assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is not true for all choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5590d608ffe24233396eb2e4f8ca142ae42963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> be the minimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> fails for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> be the minimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/9933fd19033d30ae11be4204b963a2ea0b0627b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_0,k}\\leq x_{i_0,1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />. Then it must be the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6796561a868d155de11c0431f54d42651747e4a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_0\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31765ce9dc9608a271dfc4bbacfd7e30e34c72f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> be a shortest sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1d3a133633b070f741bd763d43b2e9c47f0fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_0,k_0} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> integers that the frog occupies in jumping from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52fe5e34fb333de4a4a31a86f71d2189769860f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" />. The length of each jump, that is, the difference between consecutive integers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" />, is either 1 or a positive integer power of 2. The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> cannot contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851379e73a11f6152d14fb140886f7adf9341dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{t_0}$\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> because it takes more jumps to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f6a2101526ac96a79a07373d6194d6328ee3a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{t_0} k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> than it does to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851379e73a11f6152d14fb140886f7adf9341dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{t_0}$\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fdafc84888b565619925e6038e30a877d6099b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{M+1}$\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/5323631f8fac5004aad3cb8962f0c06c3f2cf9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> be the length of the longest jump made in generating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" />. Such a jump can only be made from a number that is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26efa3b2a66022822997a7aa2808cac4aa3d4fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^M$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> (and by no higher power of 2). Thus we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5de3e7e2c5bb672e0bd0c43afcf4d3fd1bfc7e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M &lt; i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, since otherwise a number divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is visited before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52fe5e34fb333de4a4a31a86f71d2189769860f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> is reached, contradicting the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e942790378476e4ea1c95e170bacf8e074fe3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m+1}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> be the length of the jump when the frog jumps over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. If this jump starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a09e58fd0939025525fe164d5ee36c56926c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m(2t - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, then it will end at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16a7a5916901a5d51c95b5858cb59a46146dc31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m(2t - 1) + 2^{m+1} = 2^m(2t + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"249\" height=\"19\" />. Since it goes over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b837fddf8e7b946133c1f19968360312be75c41a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m(2t - 1) &lt; 2^{i_0} &lt; 2^m(2t + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dffc710d4d5b23bc08f9af3d9717abe6a2e12669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{i_0-m} - 1)/2 &lt; t &lt; (2^{i_0-m} + 1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"19\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df210f3256e90f59d4dbb9fb9b67f42bae3b593b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 2^{i_0-m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> and the jump over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f53d233f86395080e7ff58be34a2706de732e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m(2^{i_0-m} - 1) = 2^{i_0} - 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"19\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e72b13b2acff36dec8b7e71a9c8a84b2d274baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m(2^{i_0-m}+1) = 2^{i_0} + 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Considering the jumps that generate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535f2647ce093bccd2a78a1174e6714a1d035a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the number of jumps from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66faf5a3a41aa8e5f895dc5bf87587eb7589679d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} + 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e715db9bdeefe6c4f6b079451b994061a92e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the number of jumps from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66faf5a3a41aa8e5f895dc5bf87587eb7589679d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} + 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e50b12b20eaf120e3f9423dfc31e7c52f190c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />. By definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5590d608ffe24233396eb2e4f8ca142ae42963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> can be reached from 1 in less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535f2647ce093bccd2a78a1174e6714a1d035a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> jumps. On the other hand, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b843095617e8a50411a8f14a043d6a151d9468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b46698d32e8bc55957ddf1f52f4476ce9f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}(k_0 - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"19\" /> can be reached from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e715db9bdeefe6c4f6b079451b994061a92e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> jumps by using the same jump length sequence as in jumping from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0e852a172969d1dd53f653ab29228c40ab6dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m + 2^{i_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2f18e424ef3bd6a597c53895cbd5fd553bce98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} k_0 = 2^{i_0}(k_0 - 1) + 2^{i_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"22\" />. The key point here is that the shift by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> does not affect any of divisibility conditions needed to make jumps of the same length. In particular, with the exception of the last entry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52fe5e34fb333de4a4a31a86f71d2189769860f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" />, all of the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa7f201e016afed373751c9ede9b6db399e270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_{i_0,k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1881d49d9cbec1561d4c08c1350da34a341c96ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^p(2t + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe3afa746fc23bcc68df54a02c3580996228379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />, again because of the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd68092d1a309ac379bb37a040dc0d2fb28f212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^p(2t + 1) - 2^{i_0} = 2^p(2t - 2^{i_0-p} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"19\" /> and the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b64d1bbf1f3acdb962d1a6bcb082e7b507a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2t + 2^{i_0-p} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> is odd, a jump of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc2563ea1c21bcf72b13f6cecfef9c8427ca21fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{p+1}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> can be made from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d83d03c6c4570de33dff211870df281ae6001a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^p(2t + 1) - 2^{i_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" /> just as it can be made from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1881d49d9cbec1561d4c08c1350da34a341c96ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^p(2t + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the frog can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> from 1 in less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535f2647ce093bccd2a78a1174e6714a1d035a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> jumps, and can then reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b46698d32e8bc55957ddf1f52f4476ce9f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}(k_0 - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"19\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e715db9bdeefe6c4f6b079451b994061a92e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> jumps. Hence the frog can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b46698d32e8bc55957ddf1f52f4476ce9f3192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}(k_0 - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"19\" /> from 1 in less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a71d64e56f7102b3fae4f1d80cb3e97385d44c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1 + N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> jumps, that is, in fewer jumps than needed to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52fe5e34fb333de4a4a31a86f71d2189769860f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0} k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> and hence in fewer jumps than required to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96e92e3c0940a71f71eddfeba9030d83e2fb753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{i_0}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. This contradicts the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d17e246dd87ce601d517794c959583040822053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 1, x_1, \\ldots, x_t = 2^i k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> are the integers visited by the frog on his trip from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b02852649c50d92f54657e47ef1c684ae99b48b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i k$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a0ef476cf5452cdb5a980c9697dc1068e0731b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b490ae60187647b15cbf6ebe6f5f645b1af264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_j = x_j - x_{j-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"12\" /> be the jump sizes. Define a reduced path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c472b0981d0e017b3914f324344a888c22607c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> inductively by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/f/98fd2c2a8d22f9741491603227b2101027d67a5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_j = \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} y_{j-1} + s_j &amp; \\text{if }y_{j-1} + s_j\\leq 2^i, \\\\ y_{j-1} &amp; \\text{otherwise.} \\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"43\" />\nSay a jump <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/8095b5ffad3782e13b04e499290a1dca1600bc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is deleted in the second case. We will show that the distinct integers among the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c472b0981d0e017b3914f324344a888c22607c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> give a shorter path from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b92d67419c77c7a9bab9103274256eb1ba428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i$\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d30cc1b0950aca1acc6938d5590b40af01ed751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j\\leq 2^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fdca9647cc9a55f0e32229b2f19f2b3a5cc3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i - 2^{r+1} &lt; y_j\\leq 2^i - 2^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47cd5c3ed716a4636c0cc56769285b393b3e20f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq r\\leq i - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. Then every deleted jump before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c472b0981d0e017b3914f324344a888c22607c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> must have length greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d230fae6558a1a3ada3c4452aeb2561e9a0e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, hence must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2263ccce98dc7c0f514870f3eddf9debaebb47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{r+1}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad000785e905b92fb74330eaf2ae6e72aed7541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j\\equiv x_j\\pmod{2^{r+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2d3b53541947aa93ce61ec9c8f7ed596eb3a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{j+1} &gt; y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, then either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883f1d1c6394c92ff96cfdec2cad4a08d5159a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{j+1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> (in which case this is a valid jump) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5285580d2af21964eb842cad72d6371257947af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{j+1}/2 = 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> is the exact power of 2 dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0e6fa105993ce976db0dc241d59ab8e68e6efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. In the second case, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59dd1b29daaabbd47536dadaf4004fc193b38132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^r\\geq s_{j+1} &gt; 2^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, the congruence says <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> is also the exact power of 2 dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c472b0981d0e017b3914f324344a888c22607c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, thus again this is a valid jump. Thus the distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c472b0981d0e017b3914f324344a888c22607c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> form a valid path for the frog. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1cea27cbb273f1406f9203aed0a223b5ad03f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> the congruence gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b8fad8e4156d03ebe499297477114a000e55f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_t\\equiv x_t\\equiv 0\\pmod{2^{r+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"19\" />, but this is impossible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0b4b3a2ed197d377bb12ac9b91ee79ff8d673b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i - 2^{r+1} &lt; y_t\\leq 2^i - 2^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />. Hence we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e49ff008be314f663714f04c6a7fe36f1edd92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_t = 2^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, that is, the reduced path ends at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b92d67419c77c7a9bab9103274256eb1ba428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i$\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />. Finally since the reduced path ends at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b2284507753b8ddac3ea822c1b3c54187e1c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^i &lt; 2^i k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> at least one jump must have been deleted and it is strictly shorter than the original path.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=84558 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO\" title=\"2006 USAMO\">2006 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016232809\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPre